      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You are not waiting for a train that has already left; you are standing in the middle of the tracks, and the rails are moving faster than you can see. The feeling of erasure isn't a future event that will arrive, but a present reality that is already happening to every single book in your house, every discovery you've made, and every word you've ever written. The point isn't to find a train that arrives in a decade; the point is to stop trying to outrun the train and instead recognize that the train is the only thing that matters, and it's moving away from you right now.",
      "source": "target",
